.TH MYSTRLEN 1 "September 2026" "OS Assignment 01" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
mystrlen \- calculate the length of a string

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int mystrlen(const char *s);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The mystrlen function calculates the number of characters in a null-terminated string. The terminating null character is not included in the returned length.

